wined3d: the GLSL blitter draws a P8 surface to the drawable without an attachable format

glsl_blitter_supported() declined any blit whose destination format is
not FBO-attachable and not a render target, also when the destination
location is the drawable, which renders into the window's framebuffer and
never attaches the texture. Without ARB_texture_rg (OpenGL 2.1, the V3D's
desktop profile on a Raspberry Pi 4) P8 is GL_ALPHA8, not attachable: the
front buffer of an 8-bit DirectDraw game went to the CPU blitter, which
loads the drawable again, which blits again -- an endless recursion and a
stack overflow (StarCraft, an 8 bpp DirectDraw test).

The attachability is checked only for blits to a texture location; an
8 bpp DirectDraw test now shows its colour bars and grey ramp exactly.

--- a/dlls/wined3d/glsl_shader.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/glsl_shader.c
@@ -12878,7 +12878,11 @@
         return FALSE;
     }
 
-    if (!((dst_format->caps[WINED3D_GL_RES_TYPE_TEX_2D] & WINED3D_FORMAT_CAP_FBO_ATTACHABLE)
+    /* A blit to the drawable renders into the window's framebuffer, not into the texture: a P8 front buffer
+     * (GL_ALPHA8 without ARB_texture_rg, not attachable) is drawn through the palette that way. Declined, it
+     * went to the CPU blitter, which loads the drawable again, which blits again: endless recursion on GL 2.1. */
+    if (dst_location != WINED3D_LOCATION_DRAWABLE
+            && !((dst_format->caps[WINED3D_GL_RES_TYPE_TEX_2D] & WINED3D_FORMAT_CAP_FBO_ATTACHABLE)
             || (dst_resource->bind_flags & WINED3D_BIND_RENDER_TARGET)))
     {
         TRACE("Destination texture is not FBO attachable.\n");
